## Differences and action plan

D1. contract.md Realizations does not match contract.json (documentation, fix in the contract). `## Realizations -> Web` still says "Not started. Planned: ..." and `### Coverage` says "None yet", while `realizations.web` is `complete` with 14 coverage lines. `### Known drift` lists 6 entries; the JSON has 12. Missing in the md: axe `scrollable-region-focusable` filter (owner decision 2026-11-12), empty state also `aria-hidden`, first enabled item active on load, mousedown prevented on items, manual filter never hides groups/separators, 500 ms announcement debounce. Action: regenerate or update contract.md Realizations (Web, Coverage, Known drift) from the JSON. Code needs no change.

D2. Empty state exposure (drift already recorded): contract says role `none`; code also sets `aria-hidden="true"` because axe flags `aria-required-children` otherwise. Consequence: the empty text is announced only through the status region (as the contract says), so the contract and code agree in effect. Action: add the one-line note to contract.md section 9 so the "role none" wording is not read as the whole truth; keep the code.

D3. Manual filter vs "nothing hides" (drift recorded): groups and separators are never hidden in manual mode, which matches "nothing hides" literally. No gap; only the md omission (D1). One wording check for the owner: the contract's behavior text says "the empty state, the active item and the announcement still follow the items present", which the code does.

D4. `npm run check` fails O1 (outputs stale: "foundations or contracts changed since the last propagate"). The contract edit (uncommitted `spec/components/command/contract.json`) is the cause. Action: run `sketchbook propagate`, then the Figma scripts it lists, before merge. Not a component defect.

D5. Items outside the contract, small, all recorded as drift except the first: (a) `Enter` is ignored while `isComposing` (IME), not in the contract; add one line to the keyboard table or accept as implementation detail; (b) the announcement delay of 500 ms is a PROPOSAL "to confirm in review"; (c) contract status is still `draft` (correct until beta review and the owed manual screen-reader pass, Q5).

D6. Owed before beta, not a parity defect: manual VoiceOver (Safari) and NVDA (Chrome, Firefox) pass for element-reference `aria-activedescendant` (Q5); `a11y-auditor` live keyboard pass (Q4); design realization is `not-started`.

No code-versus-contract behavior divergence was found. Every drift entry is deliberate, the 12 entries in `realizations.web.drift` each correspond to observed code, and the contract-side entries are consistent with SB-0103.

## Verdict

Needs contract update. The implementation matches the contract on props, events, anatomy, filtering, keyboard, ARIA, tokens and states, with the recorded drift. The only gaps are documentation: contract.md Realizations/Coverage/Known drift are stale versus contract.json (D1, D2), plus check O1 needs `sketchbook propagate` (D4). No code fix is required.

Status (2026-11-15): fixed in this PR (contract.md Known drift gains the two entries it lacked, input method composition and browser floor); D1 rest, D2 and D4 already fixed (Realizations and Coverage match contract.json, section 9 says the empty text is not exposed in the listbox, O1 passes).
